1
00:00:28,580 --> 00:00:29,897
I'm the programmer in the world.

2
00:00:29,980 --> 00:00:31,392
I'm not gonna be guilty.

3
00:00:31,700 --> 00:00:33,112
I'm not gonna be guilty.

4
00:00:33,660 --> 00:00:34,757
I'm not gonna be guilty.

5
00:00:34,840 --> 00:00:36,620
I'm gonna be relaxed.

6
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:41,760
I'm gonna be like, I don't want to die.

7
00:00:45,180 --> 00:00:47,020
Okay, alright.

8
00:00:48,040 --> 00:00:50,020
I'm not gonna be a survivor.

9
00:00:51,080 --> 00:00:54,980
Get away from, I don't wanna die.

10
00:00:56,340 --> 00:00:57,170
Let's go.

11
00:00:57,253 --> 00:00:58,083
There you go!

12
00:00:58,166 --> 00:01:00,160
One, two, three Come and find a way!

13
00:01:00,320 --> 00:01:01,440
I find a way

14
00:01:13,500 --> 00:01:14,417
Break out

15
00:01:53,800 --> 00:01:56,918
Here is my one and only
trusted assistant, Charlotte.

16
00:01:57,200 --> 00:01:58,030
Hello.

17
00:01:59,380 --> 00:02:00,321
Charlotte, dear,

18
00:02:00,460 --> 00:02:02,397
if you would please give our prisoners a

19
00:02:02,480 --> 00:02:04,297
brief rundown of what
their lives will be like?

20
00:02:04,380 --> 00:02:05,577
for the foreseeable future.

21
00:02:05,660 --> 00:02:06,490
Sure.

22
00:02:06,600 --> 00:02:10,600
Here in this prison facility, we
represent the ideas of our country!

23
00:02:10,700 --> 00:02:12,406
placing emphasis on equality.

24
00:02:12,880 --> 00:02:15,577
If you wish to wander around
or partake in exercise,

25
00:02:15,660 --> 00:02:18,157
you are free to do so
in a designated area.

26
00:02:18,240 --> 00:02:21,358
You can use the phones, take
a shower, or read books.

27
00:02:21,600 --> 00:02:24,797
An exemplary prisoner can
even have a TV in their cell.

28
00:02:24,880 --> 00:02:28,617
Some may be allowed to work and are given
a chance to study for a college degree.

29
00:02:28,700 --> 00:02:30,700
You heard her, and that's not all.

30
00:02:31,600 --> 00:02:33,877
Ah, yes, Charlotte, do
you have a question?

31
00:02:33,960 --> 00:02:37,237
I just remembered, there are rules that
must be followed too, aren't there?

32
00:02:37,320 --> 00:02:39,817
Why, of course, Charlotte,
you're absolutely right.

33
00:02:39,900 --> 00:02:40,730
First,

34
00:02:40,813 --> 00:02:42,457
under no circumstances are
you allowed to take off

35
00:02:42,540 --> 00:02:45,437
the wristband with your
designated prisoner number.

36
00:02:45,520 --> 00:02:48,577
Second, there will be no borrowing
or lending things among inmates,

37
00:02:48,660 --> 00:02:50,954
and any metal materials are prohibited.

38
00:02:51,080 --> 00:02:52,845
Is wearing earring still okay?

39
00:02:53,040 --> 00:02:54,617
Shut your mouth right this instant!

40
00:02:54,700 --> 00:02:55,994
The chief is speaking!

41
00:02:56,540 --> 00:03:00,940
No, they're not allowed,
inmate FE40536 Joling Code.

42
00:03:01,300 --> 00:03:05,677
If you have any further inquiries, please
ask the guards and they can assist you.

43
00:03:05,760 --> 00:03:08,280
Orientation is complete! All right!

44
00:03:08,720 --> 00:03:10,896
Everyone, turn and face to your left!

45
00:03:11,540 --> 00:03:13,020
This place is huge.

46
00:03:13,400 --> 00:03:15,929
I hear the prison covers
this whole island.

47
00:03:16,080 --> 00:03:17,260
Oh, alligator.

48
00:03:30,180 --> 00:03:31,010
F .E.

49
00:03:31,093 --> 00:03:35,140
40536, welcome to your
new home, cell number 206.

50
00:03:39,700 --> 00:03:41,935
Break time for today is come and gone.

51
00:03:42,120 --> 00:03:44,300
The cell opens at 6.30 a .m.

52
00:03:44,760 --> 00:03:49,054
Breakfast begins at 7 a .m., but if
you wish to sleep in, you're allowed.

53
00:03:50,320 --> 00:03:51,908
Hope you two can get along.

54
00:03:55,420 --> 00:03:56,500
Nice to meet you.

55
00:03:57,220 --> 00:03:58,808
Yeah, nice to meet you too.

56
00:03:58,940 --> 00:03:59,999
The name's Jolene.

57
00:04:00,400 --> 00:04:02,480
My name is Gwess. Want some?

58
00:04:03,080 --> 00:04:03,910
Thank you.

59
00:04:04,340 --> 00:04:08,340
But so much stuff happened today
that I just don't have an appetite.

60
00:04:11,540 --> 00:04:12,457
What's your problem?

61
00:04:12,540 --> 00:04:14,917
I know you're new here, but
the bottom book is mine!

62
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:17,637
Are you gonna have a problem with
that, you stupid little whore?!

63
00:04:17,720 --> 00:04:18,550
Bee!

64
00:04:19,640 --> 00:04:20,520
Jojo! Bee!

65
00:04:25,700 --> 00:04:28,017
Look, I'm not interested in fighting you.

66
00:04:28,100 --> 00:04:31,571
I saw your stuff on the top
bed, so I thought it was yours.

67
00:04:33,840 --> 00:04:35,520
Why is that here?!

68
00:04:36,080 --> 00:04:37,357
What is wrong with you?!

69
00:04:37,440 --> 00:04:39,297
Now you're trying to jack my stuff too?!

70
00:04:39,380 --> 00:04:40,210
No!

71
00:04:40,293 --> 00:04:41,157
I just want to see that closer!

72
00:04:41,240 --> 00:04:42,317
Please listen to me!

73
00:04:42,400 --> 00:04:43,357
If you open that charm,

74
00:04:43,440 --> 00:04:46,417
you'll find a small stone and
a picture of my parents inside.

75
00:04:46,500 --> 00:04:48,265
It may be the one I threw away

76
00:04:49,080 --> 00:04:50,020
Is that so?

77
00:04:50,260 --> 00:04:52,917
I bought this for two bucks
from a new inmate the other day.

78
00:04:53,000 --> 00:04:54,765
It's pretty, wouldn't you say?

79
00:04:55,000 --> 00:04:55,830
Yeah, sure.

80
00:04:55,913 --> 00:04:56,743
Just let me see.

81
00:04:56,826 --> 00:04:58,117
Get your hands off me, you filthy bitch.

82
00:04:58,200 --> 00:04:59,030
No way.

83
00:04:59,113 --> 00:04:59,943
I'm letting you see it

84
00:05:01,440 --> 00:05:03,840
Fine, I'll buy it off of you. Go ahead.

85
00:05:04,040 --> 00:05:04,960
Name your price

86
00:05:05,540 --> 00:05:07,180
200 bucks. What the hell?

87
00:05:07,760 --> 00:05:10,080
Didn't you hear me dumbass? I said 200

88
00:05:11,240 --> 00:05:12,070
Bitch

89
00:05:19,340 --> 00:05:20,640
Let's out!

90
00:05:31,360 --> 00:05:33,400
The heck's up with everything?

91
00:05:33,700 --> 00:05:35,582
So many strange things happened.

92
00:05:39,240 --> 00:05:41,820
My mind is racing with thoughts.

93
00:05:43,420 --> 00:05:44,797
I hate this.

94
00:05:44,880 --> 00:05:47,040
I feel so lonely, I could cry.

95
00:05:58,160 --> 00:05:59,937
What are you doing?!

96
00:06:00,020 --> 00:06:01,500
About last night.

97
00:06:01,660 --> 00:06:03,200
I'm really sorry. Huh?

98
00:06:05,340 --> 00:06:06,170
Morning?

99
00:06:07,680 --> 00:06:08,620
Take it.

100
00:06:10,060 --> 00:06:10,890
Huh?

101
00:06:10,973 --> 00:06:12,719
Don't worry, it's fine if you look.

102
00:06:12,980 --> 00:06:16,340
Although, that pic of your
parents wasn't in there.

103
00:06:16,620 --> 00:06:19,237
Sorry, but I don't think this
is the charm you're looking for.

104
00:06:19,320 --> 00:06:20,150
See?

105
00:06:22,600 --> 00:06:25,240
Was anything inside at all? Like a stone?

106
00:06:25,480 --> 00:06:26,800
Sorry, there wasn't.

107
00:06:27,480 --> 00:06:30,421
Anyway, can you forgive
my actions from yesterday?

108
00:06:30,720 --> 00:06:32,300
You see, I'm a coward.

109
00:06:32,780 --> 00:06:34,839
Especially when meeting new people.

110
00:06:36,000 --> 00:06:36,830
It's okay.

111
00:06:37,080 --> 00:06:39,551
If anything, it was my fault for assuming.

112
00:06:39,940 --> 00:06:42,293
I'm still learning how things work here.

113
00:06:42,680 --> 00:06:44,974
Wow, Jolene, you're such a nice person.

114
00:06:45,060 --> 00:06:47,119
I hope we can become close friends.

115
00:06:47,520 --> 00:06:48,932
Yeah, I'd like that too.

116
00:06:52,240 --> 00:06:53,497
Oh, there's the buzzer.

117
00:06:53,580 --> 00:06:55,037
Looks like it's breakfast time.

118
00:06:55,120 --> 00:06:56,237
See you there, bestie.

119
00:06:56,320 --> 00:06:57,560
Hey, wait for me!

120
00:06:57,760 --> 00:06:58,936
I'm coming with you!

121
00:07:00,220 --> 00:07:01,340
Are you serious?

122
00:07:01,580 --> 00:07:03,345
What's up with all this water?

123
00:07:04,400 --> 00:07:06,380
My pants are soaking wet now!

124
00:07:06,500 --> 00:07:07,618
What am I gonna do?

125
00:07:15,120 --> 00:07:18,217
Excuse me, but what do you mean
the food's sold out already?

126
00:07:18,300 --> 00:07:19,737
I haven't even had my meal yet!

127
00:07:19,820 --> 00:07:20,937
Can't you see it's gone?

128
00:07:21,020 --> 00:07:23,017
Here at GD, you've got
the freedom to sleep in,

129
00:07:23,100 --> 00:07:25,117
just like you have the
freedom to arrive late.

130
00:07:25,200 --> 00:07:27,117
Shouldn't you have food
prepared for everyone?

131
00:07:27,200 --> 00:07:29,277
You've got to at least have a banana left!

132
00:07:29,360 --> 00:07:31,897
That's what we call one of
the Seven Wonders of Prison.

133
00:07:31,980 --> 00:07:33,156
What does that mean?

134
00:07:33,740 --> 00:07:36,220
Oh, Jolyne, guess you decided to sleep in.

135
00:07:36,320 --> 00:07:38,732
I'm so full, I couldn't eat another bite.

136
00:07:41,980 --> 00:07:43,000
Glass, hold on!

137
00:07:43,180 --> 00:07:46,097
Did I just see two milks and
two bananas on your tray?

138
00:07:46,180 --> 00:07:47,010
No way.

139
00:07:47,093 --> 00:07:48,275
Why would I have two?

140
00:07:48,360 --> 00:07:49,419
That'd be selfish.

141
00:07:49,680 --> 00:07:53,057
Oh, by the way, sorry about all
the water I spilled on the floor.

142
00:07:53,140 --> 00:07:55,037
Don't worry, I'll clean it all up later.

143
00:07:55,120 --> 00:07:56,649
I already took care of it.

144
00:07:56,920 --> 00:07:58,508
Wow, that's so nice of you.

145
00:07:58,600 --> 00:07:59,953
Thanks a bunch, Jolyne.

146
00:08:04,900 --> 00:08:06,180
Wait, this is...

147
00:08:13,600 --> 00:08:14,776
This is your chance.

148
00:08:14,980 --> 00:08:16,477
Fly over here and take a look.

149
00:08:16,560 --> 00:08:18,657
I believe you can do it with all my heart.

150
00:08:18,740 --> 00:08:20,937
You can do anything
with the power of love.

151
00:08:21,020 --> 00:08:24,432
Yes, as long as we trust each
other, anything is possible.

152
00:08:25,380 --> 00:08:26,540
Now give it a try.

153
00:08:34,000 --> 00:08:35,137
You're so freaking adorable.

154
00:08:35,220 --> 00:08:37,338
I knew you could pull it off for me.

155
00:08:37,560 --> 00:08:38,390
Coffee chop!

156
00:08:38,473 --> 00:08:39,342
That was great!

157
00:08:39,840 --> 00:08:41,487
Here, have a treat, darling!

158
00:08:41,640 --> 00:08:42,470
Good morning!

159
00:08:44,920 --> 00:08:46,626
Now, we've talked about this.

160
00:08:46,740 --> 00:08:48,417
You don't greet me with good morning.

161
00:08:48,500 --> 00:08:49,912
It's love you, remember?

162
00:08:50,160 --> 00:08:51,237
Now, let's try again.

163
00:08:51,320 --> 00:08:53,897
It's much cuter when you
say you love me, you know?

164
00:08:53,980 --> 00:08:55,080
I love you!

165
00:08:55,600 --> 00:08:56,430
Yes!

166
00:08:56,513 --> 00:08:57,357
Good, good, good, good, good!

167
00:08:57,440 --> 00:08:59,911
That's my perfect little man, coffee chop!

168
00:09:01,220 --> 00:09:02,514
Now, something harder.

169
00:09:02,780 --> 00:09:04,192
Try flying to my finger.

170
00:09:04,880 --> 00:09:09,292
To build trust between us, we have to
take risks here and there, Kapi-Chan.

171
00:09:10,640 --> 00:09:11,637
What's wrong with you?

172
00:09:11,720 --> 00:09:12,896
Just get on with it!

173
00:09:16,960 --> 00:09:17,920
What? Whoa?

174
00:09:19,220 --> 00:09:20,640
What did you just say?

175
00:09:20,880 --> 00:09:23,762
Do little birdies say,
whoa, where you come from?

176
00:09:27,320 --> 00:09:29,791
Hey, now, don't you start messing with me.

177
00:09:29,900 --> 00:09:32,957
Do you got some superficial idea
about what love and trust should be?

178
00:09:33,040 --> 00:09:34,420
Huh? Do you?

179
00:09:36,500 --> 00:09:38,360
Well, you've broken that trust.

180
00:09:38,960 --> 00:09:40,019
I'm done with you.

181
00:09:43,700 --> 00:09:45,400
Did something just go by?

182
00:09:47,520 --> 00:09:48,480
A banana?

183
00:09:55,100 --> 00:09:57,280
What is up with this weird bird?

184
00:10:10,060 --> 00:10:10,960
No way.

185
00:10:11,500 --> 00:10:13,420
Small, but it has to be real.

186
00:10:16,000 --> 00:10:19,780
There's a tiny person
inside, and she killed them!

187
00:10:39,320 --> 00:10:40,820
Glass. That woman.

188
00:10:43,440 --> 00:10:47,177
The only explanation for this is
she has that stone from the amulet,

189
00:10:47,260 --> 00:10:49,397
and it gave her some
kind of special ability.

190
00:10:49,480 --> 00:10:52,009
But what the hell is
with that small human?

191
00:11:03,640 --> 00:11:04,470
Wha...

192
00:11:04,553 --> 00:11:05,860
What is going on now?

193
00:11:13,700 --> 00:11:14,530
Wha...

194
00:11:14,613 --> 00:11:15,443
What the hell?

195
00:11:15,526 --> 00:11:16,537
My body...

196
00:11:16,620 --> 00:11:17,738
Did it just shrink?

197
00:11:17,940 --> 00:11:19,380
So the culprit was you.

198
00:11:22,600 --> 00:11:25,620
How did you take my
copychan away from me?!

199
00:11:28,780 --> 00:11:31,420
Jolene! Jolene! Jolene! Jolene!

200
00:11:36,420 --> 00:11:38,957
Jolene, I'm starting to
like you more and more.

201
00:11:39,040 --> 00:11:40,687
I knew we'd be good friends.

202
00:11:40,920 --> 00:11:42,626
What's going on with my body?

203
00:11:42,840 --> 00:11:43,781
What did you do?

204
00:11:44,040 --> 00:11:45,216
Hey, Jolene, listen.

205
00:11:45,440 --> 00:11:47,337
I need you to stop talking, okay?

206
00:11:47,420 --> 00:11:49,479
I'm like that person in the parrot!

207
00:11:49,800 --> 00:11:51,500
I said stop talking!

208
00:11:53,220 --> 00:11:54,160
Put this on!

209
00:11:55,160 --> 00:11:56,984
I already removed all the guts.

210
00:11:57,800 --> 00:11:59,800
The parrot had some disadvantages.

211
00:12:00,160 --> 00:12:02,807
The poor thing couldn't
hold or carry things.

212
00:12:03,040 --> 00:12:04,216
But rats are better.

213
00:12:04,460 --> 00:12:05,754
They've got four paws.

214
00:12:06,680 --> 00:12:09,974
As for him, he was a guard
who got fired for being lazy.

215
00:12:10,440 --> 00:12:13,440
The chief and everyone
thinks he already went home.

216
00:12:16,400 --> 00:12:19,280
And by the way, I know
I told you not to speak,

217
00:12:19,440 --> 00:12:22,197
but I'll let it slide if
you do it in a cutesy way.

218
00:12:22,280 --> 00:12:23,357
Mike, see you later.

219
00:12:23,440 --> 00:12:24,377
Oh, Mommy, I'm hungry.

220
00:12:24,460 --> 00:12:25,380
Please feed me.

221
00:12:25,740 --> 00:12:26,860
Yeah, okay?

222
00:12:29,160 --> 00:12:31,240
Look at you, so stinking adorable.

223
00:12:32,080 --> 00:12:33,904
Now, let's begin your training.

224
00:12:35,400 --> 00:12:37,240
Faster, faster, faster, faster!

225
00:12:39,560 --> 00:12:40,800
Show me some hustle!

226
00:12:44,200 --> 00:12:45,980
Now lift them up, Chorokichi.

227
00:12:47,220 --> 00:12:48,050
Chorokichi?

228
00:12:48,240 --> 00:12:50,122
Everything has a name, you know.

229
00:12:50,280 --> 00:12:53,037
In the beginning was the Word,
and the Word was with God.

230
00:12:53,120 --> 00:12:55,937
And the Word was God, and
through Him all was made.

231
00:12:56,020 --> 00:12:58,897
And without Him nothing was
made that had been made.

232
00:12:58,980 --> 00:13:02,098
So this mental power that
shrank you deserves a name.

233
00:13:02,380 --> 00:13:03,880
How about Jojo Dolls?

234
00:13:04,300 --> 00:13:07,124
Yes, that will be the
name of my mental ability.

235
00:13:07,240 --> 00:13:08,660
Let's add another book.

236
00:13:12,660 --> 00:13:13,600
Naughty girl.

237
00:13:14,780 --> 00:13:17,420
Are you being cunning and trying to cheat?

238
00:13:18,040 --> 00:13:21,280
Hey now, you're not gonna
betray my trust, are you?

239
00:13:23,040 --> 00:13:26,099
You're not trying to ruin
our relationship, are you?

240
00:13:27,140 --> 00:13:28,617
I'm just messing with you.

241
00:13:28,700 --> 00:13:30,437
Congrats, Todokichi, you passed.

242
00:13:30,520 --> 00:13:33,177
You're going to need that
cunning wit for your next task.

243
00:13:33,260 --> 00:13:34,680
Very, very good!

244
00:13:40,160 --> 00:13:40,990
Can you see?

245
00:13:41,720 --> 00:13:45,237
At the far end of this corridor,
you're going to find a control center.

246
00:13:45,320 --> 00:13:47,797
Your objective is to get
to that switch over there.

247
00:13:47,880 --> 00:13:50,697
It can unlock all the cells
and doors in this prison.

248
00:13:50,780 --> 00:13:52,260
I know you can make it.

249
00:13:53,100 --> 00:13:54,497
You understand what I'm saying?

250
00:13:54,580 --> 00:13:56,639
If we work together, we can escape.

251
00:13:57,720 --> 00:14:00,277
For some reason, I can't
make myself smaller.

252
00:14:00,360 --> 00:14:02,197
Though luckily, we have you now.

253
00:14:02,280 --> 00:14:04,217
But it's important we trust each other.

254
00:14:04,300 --> 00:14:07,337
Of course, the actual
commencement is further ahead.

255
00:14:07,420 --> 00:14:12,067
For this mission, you just need to
investigate everything beyond this corridor.

256
00:14:12,220 --> 00:14:14,577
Do you really think we
can escape like this?

257
00:14:14,660 --> 00:14:15,490
Hey, hey, hey!

258
00:14:15,600 --> 00:14:19,129
Don't go forgetting I told you
to speak in a cutesy way now!

259
00:14:21,300 --> 00:14:22,720
This control center?

260
00:14:22,940 --> 00:14:25,646
How exactly am I supposed
to crawl over to it?

261
00:14:25,780 --> 00:14:27,020
You're such a Code!

262
00:14:27,300 --> 00:14:29,340
That's my adorable baby rat girl!

263
00:14:29,660 --> 00:14:31,680
But don't ask me, you dumbass.

264
00:14:32,180 --> 00:14:34,239
Figuring that part out is your job.

265
00:14:34,680 --> 00:14:35,597
Look above you.

266
00:14:35,680 --> 00:14:37,097
There's a surveillance camera.

267
00:14:37,180 --> 00:14:39,917
You'll be in its blind spot
if you go under the handrail.

268
00:14:40,000 --> 00:14:44,300
So just go straight below it
and keep the rat corpse on.

269
00:14:52,360 --> 00:14:53,760
Okay, hurry up and go!

270
00:15:05,940 --> 00:15:06,770
Hey!

271
00:15:06,853 --> 00:15:07,977
What are you doing over there?

272
00:15:08,060 --> 00:15:09,297
Girl with the headband!

273
00:15:09,380 --> 00:15:10,210
Who are you?

274
00:15:10,680 --> 00:15:12,798
Tell me your name and prison number!

275
00:15:13,160 --> 00:15:16,457
The number's FE18081, and my name is Wes.

276
00:15:16,540 --> 00:15:19,937
I'm just taking a walk around
the corridors if you don't

277
00:15:20,020 --> 00:15:23,255
have any business here get
away from the gate and leave

278
00:15:23,580 --> 00:15:24,780
Sure, mr.

279
00:15:24,900 --> 00:15:25,730
Guard

280
00:15:33,100 --> 00:15:35,137
There are four steel doors in here.

281
00:15:35,220 --> 00:15:37,557
I wonder which one of
them leads to the control

282
00:15:37,640 --> 00:15:40,920
center and there are cameras
in the corner two of them?

283
00:15:42,860 --> 00:15:45,237
What the why is it so tight! I...

284
00:15:45,320 --> 00:15:48,020
suddenly...

285
00:15:50,160 --> 00:15:50,990
Huh?

286
00:15:51,073 --> 00:15:52,617
What the hell was that sound just now?

287
00:15:52,700 --> 00:15:54,347
Yeah, man, I heard that too.

288
00:15:54,840 --> 00:15:55,670
It's close.

289
00:15:57,540 --> 00:15:59,120
Oh crap, that's not good.

290
00:15:59,300 --> 00:16:00,771
My body's getting bigger!

291
00:16:01,140 --> 00:16:02,728
It was just a coffee maker.

292
00:16:02,840 --> 00:16:04,697
Ain't that the sound it
makes when it's ready?

293
00:16:04,780 --> 00:16:05,610
Uh-uh.

294
00:16:05,693 --> 00:16:06,523
That sounds like something else.

295
00:16:06,606 --> 00:16:07,769
Why is this happening now?

296
00:16:09,020 --> 00:16:09,850
Distance.

297
00:16:10,740 --> 00:16:12,360
Is it because Quest left?

298
00:16:12,580 --> 00:16:14,639
Is distance related to her ability?

299
00:16:16,520 --> 00:16:17,920
I definitely heard it!

300
00:16:18,140 --> 00:16:19,677
It's gotta be in here somewhere!

301
00:16:19,760 --> 00:16:21,140
Shit! Shit! Shit!

302
00:16:21,880 --> 00:16:23,233
It's coming from there!

303
00:16:23,320 --> 00:16:25,380
Hey, get out of the way! Move it!

304
00:16:27,560 --> 00:16:28,390
Ah!

305
00:16:28,473 --> 00:16:29,595
That's freaking hard!

306
00:16:30,180 --> 00:16:31,480
Damn it, YB!

307
00:16:33,840 --> 00:16:34,670
Huh?

308
00:16:34,940 --> 00:16:38,677
I told you idiots it was the coffee
maker, but you wouldn't listen!

309
00:16:38,760 --> 00:16:39,590
My bad.

310
00:16:40,940 --> 00:16:42,237
Screw this investigation!

311
00:16:42,320 --> 00:16:46,026
I have to fit through the bars
before my body grows any bigger!

312
00:16:51,860 --> 00:16:53,320
What the hell?!

313
00:16:55,120 --> 00:16:57,120
Gee. Gee. Dolph.

314
00:17:07,320 --> 00:17:08,420
This thing is...

315
00:17:24,840 --> 00:17:25,670
Jojo!

316
00:17:26,120 --> 00:17:27,040
So creepy.

317
00:17:27,380 --> 00:17:29,457
It seems like a doll,
but it's transparent.

318
00:17:29,540 --> 00:17:30,599
Same as my thread.

319
00:17:30,860 --> 00:17:34,837
It's a physical manifestation of
Gwess' energy that no one else can see!

320
00:17:34,920 --> 00:17:36,780
How about Jojo dolls?

321
00:17:37,220 --> 00:17:40,017
Yes, that will be the
name of my mental ability.

322
00:17:40,100 --> 00:17:42,257
This baby doll from hell is what shrunk me

323
00:17:42,340 --> 00:17:45,046
and ripped the guard and
the parrot to pieces!

324
00:17:46,780 --> 00:17:50,437
That must mean it was just chilling
inside the rat with me the entire time!

325
00:17:50,520 --> 00:17:54,677
And I'm willing to bet that Gwess has no
idea her ability weakens if she's far away,

326
00:17:54,760 --> 00:17:57,289
so she doesn't know my
body's growing back!

327
00:17:57,720 --> 00:17:59,957
Now I've got a murderous
munchkin chasing me

328
00:18:00,040 --> 00:18:02,157
down because it thinks
that I was running away!

329
00:18:02,240 --> 00:18:05,416
If I don't get out of here,
the thing's gonna kill me!

330
00:18:10,900 --> 00:18:12,560
G. Damn it. G.

331
00:18:13,360 --> 00:18:14,190
Dolls.

332
00:18:14,320 --> 00:18:17,085
What did I ever do to
deserve a fate like this?

333
00:18:17,280 --> 00:18:18,477
This is how I go out?

334
00:18:18,560 --> 00:18:19,560
By this creature?

335
00:18:22,140 --> 00:18:23,520
I can't get through!

336
00:18:29,000 --> 00:18:30,380
G. G.

337
00:18:31,360 --> 00:18:32,190
G.

338
00:18:57,760 --> 00:18:58,590
A thread.

339
00:18:58,840 --> 00:19:00,546
No, a whole clump of threads.

340
00:19:03,960 --> 00:19:07,040
This must be the form that
my energy takes. A clump.

341
00:19:08,340 --> 00:19:11,277
When they gather and clump,
it becomes three-dimensional.

342
00:19:11,360 --> 00:19:12,400
What a concept!

343
00:19:16,160 --> 00:19:18,137
Scream your heart out, bastard child!

344
00:19:18,220 --> 00:19:20,520
Now call Gwess over here and hurry up!

345
00:19:20,900 --> 00:19:25,060
Jolene, I wasn't expecting
you to also have an ability.

346
00:19:25,580 --> 00:19:26,410
Come here!

347
00:19:27,400 --> 00:19:29,897
Wait a second, please,
Jolene, I'm begging you!

348
00:19:29,980 --> 00:19:32,197
Stop strangling my GG doll so tightly!

349
00:19:32,280 --> 00:19:33,537
Hey, I don't want to hear it!

350
00:19:33,620 --> 00:19:36,337
Focus on shrinking my body enough
so I can squeeze out of here,

351
00:19:36,420 --> 00:19:38,097
but only just a little, got it?

352
00:19:38,180 --> 00:19:41,097
Okay, okay, you can even
have the bottom bunk, too.

353
00:19:41,180 --> 00:19:44,417
I know we've been through a
lot, but please don't hate me.

354
00:19:44,500 --> 00:19:47,677
Still, though, I'd like you to speak
to me all cutesy from time to time.

355
00:19:47,760 --> 00:19:49,466
Just hurry and do it already!

356
00:19:52,480 --> 00:19:53,310
Uh, alright.

357
00:19:53,780 --> 00:19:55,217
Now hand over the amulet.

358
00:19:55,300 --> 00:19:59,097
That includes the stone inside, and I
want to know who you bought it from, too.

359
00:19:59,180 --> 00:20:00,827
Of course, whatever you say.

360
00:20:01,180 --> 00:20:02,240
That'll be $200.

361
00:20:02,600 --> 00:20:04,097
Shut the fuck up, you bitch!

362
00:20:04,180 --> 00:20:05,977
Just tell me the name before I kill you!

363
00:20:06,060 --> 00:20:07,180
Okay, I got it.

364
00:20:07,400 --> 00:20:11,640
Well, uh, I'm not sure, but I
think her name was Hermes. Hermes?

365
00:20:12,340 --> 00:20:14,000
I don't know her that well.

366
00:20:14,740 --> 00:20:15,570
Here.

367
00:20:21,940 --> 00:20:22,770
Kidding.

368
00:20:27,480 --> 00:20:28,310
Gotcha!

369
00:20:28,860 --> 00:20:30,260
Oh, Mr. Guard!

370
00:20:30,420 --> 00:20:31,540
Hurry, come here!

371
00:20:31,940 --> 00:20:34,116
There's a prisoner past the gunpoint!

372
00:20:34,660 --> 00:20:36,440
Hurry up and get over here!

373
00:20:38,140 --> 00:20:40,552
Hey you, the hell are you doing in there?

374
00:20:41,620 --> 00:20:43,267
How'd you get past the door?

375
00:20:46,540 --> 00:20:47,980
Prison break! Code 999!

376
00:20:53,100 --> 00:20:54,982
This is gonna be the end of you!

377
00:20:55,180 --> 00:20:56,010
If you didn't know,

378
00:20:56,093 --> 00:20:59,157
that guard just went to pick up his
shotgun and since you're behind the door,

379
00:20:59,240 --> 00:21:01,157
he's got the right to shoot your ass!

380
00:21:01,240 --> 00:21:02,900
No questions asked!

381
00:21:04,600 --> 00:21:05,430
Jolene!

382
00:21:05,513 --> 00:21:06,877
I'd say it's just what you deserve!

383
00:21:06,960 --> 00:21:10,136
You hurt my feelings, and
now you're gonna die for it!

384
00:21:11,900 --> 00:21:14,580
Good freakin' grief, Quest. Shut up!

385
00:21:14,740 --> 00:21:17,975
And listen, you said everything
has a name, didn't you?

386
00:21:18,180 --> 00:21:20,004
Then I'll name my ability, too.

387
00:21:20,460 --> 00:21:25,166
It'll be Stone Ocean, cause somehow I'm
gonna free myself from the Sea of Stone.

388
00:21:26,740 --> 00:21:27,817
Did you hear me?

389
00:21:27,900 --> 00:21:30,120
Stone Ocean, that's the name.

390
00:21:35,700 --> 00:21:36,530
Hold on!

391
00:21:39,440 --> 00:21:41,817
If there's some sort of
hierarchy in this prison,

392
00:21:41,900 --> 00:21:43,617
then I'll follow it as much as I need to.

393
00:21:43,700 --> 00:21:46,477
But I'm the one who's gonna
be giving out orders here.

394
00:21:46,560 --> 00:21:50,031
Now shrink me down and get me
the hell out of this hallway!

395
00:21:51,640 --> 00:21:52,470
Huh?

396
00:21:52,553 --> 00:21:53,700
Hold on, where did she go?

397
00:21:55,100 --> 00:21:55,930
She's gone!

398
00:21:57,140 --> 00:21:59,022
Are you really sure you saw her?

399
00:21:59,260 --> 00:22:01,657
Well, yeah, but I only
saw her from the back.

400
00:22:01,740 --> 00:22:02,780
Weird.

401
00:22:13,740 --> 00:22:14,570
Old man.

402
00:22:31,740 --> 00:22:35,640
My head is filled with hope.

403
00:22:36,740 --> 00:22:43,740
Of some place other than here.

404
00:22:46,540 --> 00:22:50,120
Although you think I smile.

405
00:22:51,820 --> 00:22:55,280
Inside and all the while.

406
00:22:57,020 --> 00:23:03,580
I'm wondering about my destiny.

407
00:23:05,920 --> 00:23:07,837
I'm thinking

408
00:23:07,920 --> 00:23:13,077
about all

409
00:23:13,160 --> 00:23:19,380
the things I'd like to do?

410
00:23:21,360 --> 00:23:24,417
In my life,

411
00:23:24,500 --> 00:23:29,080
I'm a dreamer,

412
00:23:29,560 --> 00:23:34,377
a distant dreamer,

413
00:23:34,460 --> 00:23:38,197
dreaming far

414
00:23:38,280 --> 00:23:44,420
away from today.

415
00:23:51,820 --> 00:23:52,650
Thank you.

416
00:24:19,880 --> 00:24:22,200
Thank you.
